`CaptchaValidator::getCaptchaSettings()` coerces any unknown provider to `'google'`, so when `provider='pow'` the login/forgot-password forms always failed with `config_missing` (no Google keys set). The existing module overrides (`modules/lhuser/login.php`, `modules/lhuser/forgotpassword.php`) that were meant to bypass this were never loaded — LHC requires `modules/lhuser/module.php` to activate overrides for that module, which was absent.

## Changes

- **`classes/CaptchaValidator.php`** — drop-in replacement for the LHC core class, loaded via a prepended autoloader before the core file is ever required. Adds `'pow'` to the valid provider set and delegates proof verification to `erLhcoreClassPowCaptcha::verifySubmittedProof()`. Google reCAPTCHA v3 and Turnstile logic is preserved verbatim.

- **`bootstrap/bootstrap.php`** — registers a prepended autoloader (`spl_autoload_register(..., true, true)`) that intercepts `LiveHelperChat\Validators\CaptchaValidator`:

```php
public function autoloadExt($className)
{
    if ($className === 'LiveHelperChat\\Validators\\CaptchaValidator') {
        include_once 'extension/lhcpowcaptcha/classes/CaptchaValidator.php';
    }
}
```

- **Removed** `modules/lhuser/login.php` and `modules/lhuser/forgotpassword.php` — were never activated and are now genuinely redundant; PoW validation flows through `CaptchaValidator` like the other two providers.

In 2.5.0, the connection retry logic for `BLE_ERR_CONN_ESTABLISHMENT` (0x3E) incorrectly activates when a previously-established connection drops with that reason code — which happens when the peer powers off within the first 6 connection events (the BLE LL "connection establishment phase"). This suppresses `onDisconnect` entirely, instead calling `onConnectFail` after up to 60+ seconds of retries (2 retries × 30s timeout). Applications with reconnect logic in `onDisconnect` never recover.

## Changes

- **`src/NimBLEClient.cpp`** — In `BLE_GAP_EVENT_DISCONNECT`, capture `wasConnected = (m_connStatus == CONNECTED)` before any state mutation:
  - Retry on 0x3E **only** when `!wasConnected` — i.e., the connection was never confirmed at the host level. A 0x3E on an established connection is a genuine disconnect, not a retryable establishment failure.
  - Call `onDisconnect` (not `onConnectFail`) when `wasConnected && rc == 0x3E`, so the semantics match what the application observes: a working connection that went away.
  - Apply the same `isConnectFail` flag consistently to the `deleteOnConnectFail` / `deleteOnDisconnect` deletion logic.

```cpp
// Before fix: retried on 0x3E regardless of whether connection was established
if (rc == connEstablishFailReason && pClient->m_connectFailRetryCount < pClient->m_config.connectFailRetries) { ... }

// After fix: only retry when the connection was never established
const bool wasConnected = (pClient->m_connStatus == CONNECTED);
if (rc == connEstablishFailReason && !wasConnected &&
    pClient->m_connectFailRetryCount < pClient->m_config.connectFailRetries) { ... }

const bool isConnectFail = (rc == connEstablishFailReason && !wasConnected);
if (isConnectFail) {
    pClient->m_pClientCallbacks->onConnectFail(pClient, rc);
} else {
    pClient->m_pClientCallbacks->onDisconnect(pClient, rc);  // now fires correctly for 0x3E post-connect
}
```

When `copy_directory` copies a student's project into an aggregation repo, it also copies `.git`, which Git interprets as a submodule — breaking `git push` on the destination repo.

## Changes

- **Export git log before copy** — runs `git -C <src> log --oneline > <dest>/<student>_git_log.txt 2>&1` so commit history is preserved for grading without the repo metadata. If the source isn't a git repo, the error message lands in the log file.
- **Strip `.git` after copy** — adds `rm -rf <dest>/.git` after `cp -r`, eliminating the submodule hazard.
- **Hardened command execution** — NULL-check on `popen()` return, `%255s` in `fscanf` to bound the read, and a warning log if `.git` removal fails.
- **Updated usage text** — `-dir` option now documents the `.git` exclusion and `_git_log.txt` side-effect.

```c
/* Exportar historial de git a archivo de texto para revisión */
snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "git -C %s log --oneline > %s 2>&1", src_path, git_log_path);
system(cmd);

/* Copiar directorio recursivamente */
snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "cp -r %s %s", src_path, dest_path);
/* ... copy + error check ... */

/* Eliminar directorio .git para evitar la creación de submódulos */
snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "rm -rf %s/.git", dest_path);
if (system(cmd) != 0) {
    printf("ADVERTENCIA: No se pudo eliminar el directorio .git de %s\n", dest_path);
}
```
